WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
HSBC values a SpaceX takeover of Tesla at $507 per share. That 33% premium still needs approval from half of all outstanding shares. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 674. Full self-driving version 15 is rolling out. A Texas polysilicon plant is on the table, and first principle sits with that factory bet. Michael Tindall at HSBC, in a note carried by TSLA Ming on X, treats control as the motive rather than operating logic

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.980
between the two companies. The premium is measured against Tesla's 30-day average of around $381.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:44.300
Elon Musk owns about 39% of SpaceX with 70% of its votes, and about 20% of Tesla. SpaceX

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.080
would likely be the surviving company, leaving him with roughly 60% of the combined vote.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:55.120
The note says SpaceX's larger AI and data center spending could reduce dilution in a combined

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.820
entity. Independent directors at both companies are studying a deal, with a possible announcement

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:07.723
as early as December. Tesla, in a rollout described by tech times, began issuing full self-driving

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:14.083
or FSD, version 15, with acclaimed 25 times improvement in critical safety case handling.

00:01:14.663 --> 00:01:19.483
The update adds improved navigation, reality view, and stronger driver monitoring.

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:25.223
Tesla started building reality view only months ago. The company also shared video of the

00:01:25.223 --> 00:01:27.183
system steering around a tree in the road.

00:01:28.165 --> 00:01:34.585
Nueces County, Texas is where Tesla has proposed according to EnergyNow.com, a $3.1 billion

00:01:34.585 --> 00:01:36.325
polysilicon refinery.

00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:42.185
The plant would produce solar-grade polysilicon from trichlorosylane for high-efficiency end-type

00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:42.905
solar cells.

00:01:43.385 --> 00:01:49.305
About $1.5 billion would go to engineering and construction, $1.4 billion to equipment

00:01:49.305 --> 00:01:52.485
and $183 million to utility infrastructure.

00:01:52.485 --> 00:01:58.305
spending would run from 2027 through 2030. The facility is expected to employ

00:01:58.305 --> 00:02:04.425
515 people by 2032. The application seeks a 10-year limit on taxable property

00:02:04.425 --> 00:02:10.291
value under Texas's jetty program. Fort Bend County holds the rest of a 10.1

00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:14.251
billion dollar vertically integrated solar manufacturing plan and the

00:02:14.251 --> 00:02:18.671
refinery is only the upstream piece of that chain. China currently accounts for

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:24.771
more than 90% of global solar-grade polysilicon output, so any domestic capacity cuts reliance

00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:25.871
on that single source.

00:02:26.671 --> 00:02:31.811
Vertical integration at this scale carries heavy capital intensity and long lead times, yet

00:02:31.811 --> 00:02:36.791
it locks in the first step of the cost curve before wafers, cells, and modules are even produced.

00:02:37.431 --> 00:02:41.951
If the plant reaches targeted output, Tesla would control the raw material that feeds its

00:02:41.951 --> 00:02:44.731
own solar products and potentially third-party sales.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:52.331
That shifts margin capture from module assembly back to the chemical stage, where purity and energy intensity dominate costs.

00:02:53.091 --> 00:02:59.191
A 30,000-40,000 ton annual capacity estimate would still be only a small fraction of global supply.

00:02:59.891 --> 00:03:05.431
The strategic value sits more in supply security and learning curve gains than in immediate market share.

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:11.351
The same filing notes that the refinery would complement planned solar cell production elsewhere in Texas,

00:03:11.351 --> 00:03:15.451
creating an internal loop from tri-chlorosylane to finish panels.

00:03:16.011 --> 00:03:20.151
That loop shortens the external procurement chain, but lengthens the capital recovery

00:03:20.151 --> 00:03:25.611
period, especially when memory and equipment prices for related AI hardware are also rising.

00:03:26.291 --> 00:03:30.711
The net effect on Tesla energy gross margins will depend on how quickly the plant can reach

00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:35.811
high utilization, and whether the polysilicon can be priced below imported equivalents

00:03:35.811 --> 00:03:37.851
after logistics and quality adjustments.

00:03:37.851 --> 00:03:43.791
Every incremental dollar of solar manufacturing capacity inside the United States reduces

00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:46.271
exposure to tariff risk and shipping delays.

00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:52.171
The project still sits years from first silicon, so near-term solar deployment volumes will

00:03:52.171 --> 00:03:54.431
keep relying on existing supply contracts.

00:03:55.131 --> 00:03:59.511
The decision to pursue the refinery is a long horizon bet that controlling the chemical

00:03:59.511 --> 00:04:03.911
feedstock will eventually matter more than buying finished cells at spot prices today.

00:04:03.911 --> 00:04:09.651
Elon Musk, in comments carried by the star, has vowed to increase output at Tesla's

00:04:09.651 --> 00:04:15.460
Shanghai Gigafactory even as sales have plunged. Built in Starlink is what Musk hopes Tesla

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:21.100
will offer toward the end of 2027. CarSaus reported in the same breath as the unsupervised

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:26.580
FSD link. He tied the feature to unsupervised full-self driving, so passengers have high

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:31.480
bandwidth for work and entertainment. The rollout would skip China because Starlink is

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:37.437
legal there. The CyberCab is currently the only Tesla model with Starlink hardware. Gary

00:04:37.437 --> 00:04:42.997
Black in remarks carried by Benzinga questioned how Tesla can compete with Waymo and Robotaxi

00:04:42.997 --> 00:04:49.277
operations. He predicts Waymo will lead in miles and trips. China's SC-01 Electric Roadster

00:04:49.277 --> 00:04:54.937
in a report from Inside EVs was originally slated for European sales this year. A new

00:04:54.937 --> 00:05:01.413
dedicated factory now pushes that timeline to 2027. Europe's electric vehicle or EV share,

00:05:01.413 --> 00:05:08.393
automotive news found reached 31% in October. The Scoda El Rock outsold the Tesla Model Y in the

00:05:08.393 --> 00:05:14.893
period. The Dacia Sandero is positioned to regain Europe's overall sales lead. The Tesla Model Y

00:05:14.893 --> 00:05:21.264
has faded after its record September. Neo, in figures carried by trading view, projects revenue

00:05:21.264 --> 00:05:27.404
above $15 billion this year. An analyst warned that its Onvobrand could undermine Tesla's planned

00:05:27.404 --> 00:05:33.524
luxury vehicle strategy. Elon Musk, in comments reported by Drive Tesla Canada, said cars

00:05:33.524 --> 00:05:38.304
will remain on AI4 because the computer now costs twice as much due to memory prices.

00:05:38.864 --> 00:05:45.643
He confirmed AI5 is headed to Optimus instead. The AI4.5 upgrade is mainly a ram change

00:05:45.643 --> 00:05:53.883
to LPDDR5X. Tesla trimmed the memory from 32GB to 24GB to control costs. Optimus will

00:05:53.883 --> 00:05:59.123
be Tesla's best product yet, Musk said in a Tesla North.com account, answering questions

00:05:59.123 --> 00:06:00.663
about future robot deployment.

00:06:01.303 --> 00:06:07.223
Elsewhere, Elon Musk declared AI superintelligence, while Yan Likun questioned Tesla's self-driving

00:06:07.223 --> 00:06:07.623
claims.

00:06:08.283 --> 00:06:12.403
Musk said optimist robots could work 168 hours a week in mines.

00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:17.803
Tesla vehicles let a surge in Chinese-made EVs while Korean automakers lost ground.

00:06:18.443 --> 00:06:23.143
Before we go, independent directors at both companies are still studying a SpaceX Tesla

00:06:23.143 --> 00:06:25.783
deal that could be announced as early as December.

00:06:26.423 --> 00:06:28.643
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

